@startuml
' Derived from src/nonogram/orchestrator.py:1591-2196 (generate's three branches),
' :192/:224/:261/:287 (the bounds) and :796 (repair_candidate).
title Recovery — which remedy a rejected candidate gets, by mode

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

state "generate(request)" as G {

  state "resolve name / tier / extent\ndraw seed, build Puzzle\ndeadline = monotonic() + 30.0s" as PRE
  note right of PRE
    All before the aggregate exists:
    an unusable one of the three must
    leave NOTHING behind (AC-045,
    AC-021, AC-098), and a usable one
    is fixed for the whole run.
  end note

  state "mode == image ?" as MODE <<choice>>

  ' ---------------- random / library ----------------
  state "POL-004 resample loop\nrun_bounded(puzzle.resample, bound 30)" as RESAMPLE {
    state "POL-001 regenerate loop\nrun_bounded(puzzle.regenerate, bound 30)" as REGEN {
      state "pending_repair set?" as PR <<choice>>
      state "POL-006 repair (random mode only)\nflip 1 filled + 1 empty inside the\nwitness-disagreement set, else the\nundecided mask. Pure: no rng draw." as REPAIR
      state "POL-001 redraw\nsource(*args, rng)" as REDRAW
      state "judge_candidate:\nclues -> solve -> score" as JUDGE
      state "unique?" as UQ <<choice>>
      state "consecutive_repairs >= 5 ?" as K <<choice>>

      PR --> REPAIR : yes
      PR --> REDRAW : no
      REPAIR --> JUDGE
      REDRAW --> JUDGE
      JUDGE --> UQ
      UQ --> K : no
      K --> REDRAW : yes — drop the lineage\n(MAX_CONSECUTIVE_REPAIRS)
      K --> REPAIR : no — repair again
    }
    state "in requested tier?" as TIER <<choice>>
    REGEN --> TIER : unique candidate, already scored
    TIER --> REGEN : no — discard, resample
  }

  ' ---------------- image ----------------
  state "convert ONCE\n(regenerate/resample stay at 0)" as CONV
  state "POL-002 pixel nudge\nrun_bounded(puzzle.nudge, bound 5)\nnudge(converted, cells) — always the\nORIGINAL conversion, so attempt n\ndiffers by exactly n pixels" as NUDGE
  state "POL-003: at the cap, stop altering\nthe image and report (AC-035)" as POL3

  PRE --> MODE
  MODE --> CONV : yes
  MODE --> RESAMPLE : no
  CONV --> NUDGE : not unique
  NUDGE --> POL3 : bound exhausted

  ' ---------------- the opt-in fourth remedy ----------------
  state "reveal_given_cells set?\n(default False)" as REV <<choice>>
  state "accept the run's FIRST sourced grid,\nUNALTERED, with cells of its answer\nrevealed (solver.choose_givens),\ncap = 5% of cells: 5@10x10, 20@20x20, 45@30x30.\nRe-verified by a fresh seeded solve." as REVEAL
  state "POL-005 GenerationAbandoned\n/ GivenCellsCapExceeded" as ABANDON

  POL3 --> REV
  RESAMPLE --> REV : both bounds exhausted
  REV --> REVEAL : yes
  REV --> ABANDON : no — the abandonment stands
  REVEAL --> ABANDON : cap exceeded —\npicture still unaltered
}

note bottom
  ONE counter, two reactions: every repair AND every redraw advances
  puzzle.regenerate, bounded at 30. MAX_CONSECUTIVE_REPAIRS = 5 bounds
  nothing — it only decides how that single budget is SPLIT. Setting it
  to 0 restores the pure-redraw loop exactly, down to the rng draws.

  Neither loop's counter is reset between resample rounds, so at most
  30 grids are EVER sourced per request, however the two rejection
  causes divide them up.

  Only a candidate the uniqueness check answered about is retried.
  A SolverTimeout, a SizeOutOfRange or a wiring bug travels straight
  out of run_bounded and ends the run.
end note

@enduml
